# pdx203 XNU patches, applied after the arch, SoC and OS series, one per line in application order.
# Carried from the pdx203 fork (UniXNU-prior, branch pdx203-bringup); the minimal format 2 image's set.
#
# Root authentication skipped under native-ufs-allow-unverified=1 (UniXNU-uke): APFS's FSIOC_KERNEL_ROOTAUTH needs a
# root hash iBoot and the SEP normally supply, and the signed owner-root policy is not built for this board.
zzzzzzz-offline-owner-root-auth-bypass.patch
# The CDC-ACM kernel log over the DWC3 (drivers/QcomXnuUsbDebug): the console tee and its worker thread.
zzzzzzzz-qcom-usb-debug-console.patch
zzzzzzzz-qcom-usb-debug-worker.patch
# EXITLOG: every process exit with its reason, t=<ms since boot> and, for a signal death, the crash detail
# (package/Pdx203FaultLog.c: PC, LR, fault address, ESR, shared-region slide, frame-pointer backtrace).
zzzzzzzzz-exit-log.patch
# sheng's launchd policy (package/BootWatchdogPolicy.c) without the boot progress layer.
zzzzzzzzza-launch-policy.patch
# EXECLOG: every exec with t=<ms since boot> (xpcproxy left out).
zzzzzzzzzb-exec-log.patch
# pmap-ram-wc=1: RAM asked for as Device memory is mapped Normal non-cacheable.
zzzzzzzzzc-pmap-ram-wc.patch
# A stackshot fills no more wait/turnstile entries than it counted (a panic seen with eight CPUs).
zzzzzzzzzd-stackshot-bounds.patch
# Shutdown leaves the read-only root mounted.
zzzzzzzzze-skip-ro-root-unmount.patch
# The native GPU grant: "*" (every process) and "!name" in the Adreno driver's NativeSandboxGrantProcess (upstream matches exact
# names only), and the same grant for connection ports in the kernel object filter (the WebKit GPU process maps its BOs).
zzzzzzzzzf-native-grant-wildcard.patch
zzzzzzzzzg-native-adreno-kobj-filter-grant.patch
# The board's unified-log forwarder (userland/OsLogConsole.mm) as the cached iomfb_fdr_loader job's /usr/bin executable, and the
# Enable-Private-Data logging preference, both overlays of the GPU addon (sheng-gpu-addon=1).
zzzzzzzzzh-oslog-forwarder-mounts.patch
# The jailbreak switch (amfi=0x80's bit drives unixnu_jailbreak): MAC_CHECK iterates the policies, so AMFI's signature hook still stamps
# cs_flags, then allows; unsigned and fake-signed code runs (TrollStore, Sileo). From the fork, with the iterate-then-allow fix (sa75).
zzzzzzzzzj-unixnu-jailbreak.patch
# The addon's staged apps (apps/: TrollStore, Sileo) unioned over /Applications (mount10).
zzzzzzzzzk-apps-addon-mount.patch
# The board's audio server plug-in (ShengAudio.driver) in the addon's audio/, union-mounted over /System/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/HAL
# (mount5), and the native_gpu_addon5_* status globals package/Pdx203Audio.cpp reads.
zzzzzzzzzl-audio-addon-mount.patch
# The board's PSCI halt/restart (halt_all_cpus calls native_board_halt_restart, set by package/ButtonProbe.cpp): shutdown and reboot
# work instead of timing out at IOPlatformExpert.cpp:884.
zzzzzzzzzm-halt-board.patch
# A well-known persona id (e.g. 99) that a stock device creates at setup but a fresh port never populated: created on demand so a
# root helper's persona-adopt spawn resolves instead of failing ESRCH (TrollStore's install helper, which spawns itself into persona 99).
zzzzzzzzzn-persona-wellknown.patch
# The physical page's first user mapping (process name, pid, address), which the Adreno driver asks before freeing a BO's
# owned pages. The board stub answered "mapped" for every page, so every freed BO was kept: a GPU-memory leak per app switch.
zzzzzzzzzo-pmap-page-owner.patch
# A fatal signal sent with kill() to backboardd or SpringBoard, logged with its sender (SIGLOG): the render server's unexplained SIGTERMs.
zzzzzzzzzp-signal-sender.patch
# DriverKit dext launches refused by default (driverkitd never serves them here), so a Bluetooth keyboard gets IOHIDEventDriver at once instead of after a 120 s check-in timeout.
zzzzzzzzzq-no-dext-launch.patch
